#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:103
msgid "4. Compression Effect Verification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:105
msgid ""
"After the service is started, you can verify the performance benefits of "
"the compression module through the built-in stress testing tool vllm "
"bench of vLLM. To accurately verify the real performance benefits of the "
"compression module in SSD cache hit scenarios, interference from DRAM "
"memory cache must be excluded to ensure that the tested KV cache is only "
"read from SSD. Strictly follow the test process below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:107
msgid "4.1 Stress Test Command Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:124
msgid "4.2 Result Verification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:125
msgid "**1. First Execution (Cold Start No Cache, Baseline Test)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:127
msgid ""
"First restart the vLLM service to clear all historical caches and ensure "
"the service is in a pure cold start state. After executing the stress "
"test command, no historical KV cache can be reused, and all prefix tokens"
" need to be fully prefilled and calculated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:129
msgid ""
"The Mean TTFT output by the stress test is the baseline value without "
"cache and compression optimization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:130
msgid ""
"The service log will show `hit hbm: 0, hit external: 0`, with no SSD "
"cache hit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:131
msgid ""
"Observe the `COMPRESS DUMP` related compression dump logs; the KV cache "
"generated by this request has been compressed and persisted to SSD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:133
msgid "**2. Before Second Execution: Restart Service to Clear DRAM Cache**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:135
msgid ""
"You must restart the vLLM service to completely clear the DRAM memory "
"cache in the process, ensuring that subsequent requests cannot hit the "
"cache from memory and can only read the compressed KV cache that has been"
" dumped to SSD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:137
msgid ""
"This step is the core control variable operation of the test, which "
"avoids memory cache interference on test results and verifies the pure "
"performance benefit brought by the compression module under SSD cache hit"
" scenarios."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:139
msgid "**3. Second Execution (SSD Cache Hit, Compression Effect Verification)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:141
msgid ""
"After restarting the service, immediately execute the exact same stress "
"test command as the first run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:143
msgid ""
"The Mean TTFT output by the stress test will be significantly reduced, "
"representing the end-to-end latency optimization benefit brought by the "
"compression module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:144
msgid ""
"The service log will show `hit hbm: 0, hit external: 125` (full SSD cache"
" hit) with no memory cache hit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/prefix-cache/compress_store.md:145
msgid ""
"Observe the `COMPRESS LOAD` related decompression and loading logs to "
"verify the full workflow of the compression module works properly."
msgstr ""

